00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:12.730
Yeah, it was just adorable and very, very dope.
对，那真的是太可爱也太酷了。

408
00:23:13.790 --> 00:23:19.610
And we had this ritual where, like, when we would go to dinner, I would go to her room.
我们还有一个习惯，就是每次去吃晚饭的时候，我会去她的房间。

409
00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:23.570
She would change out of her fabulously stylish outfit.
她会换下她那套时髦优雅的衣服。

410
00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:24.990
But she was shy.
但她又很害羞。

411
00:23:24.990 --> 00:23:26.710
So she would go into her walk-in closet.
所以她会走进步入式衣帽间去换衣服。

412
00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:29.350
And then we would continue to talk while she changed.
然后我们就会一边换衣服一边继续聊天。

413
00:23:29.610 --> 00:23:32.250
And when she was in the closet, her voice would be muffled like this.
当她在衣帽间里时，她的声音听起来就像这样闷声闷气的。

414
00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:34.570
And then when she came out, it would be really clear.
然后等她走出来的时候，声音就变得非常清晰。

415
00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:37.970
And so one day I'm in her room and waiting for her to change.
所以有一天我在她房间里等她换衣服。

416
00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:41.610
And I am playing with the stuff on her dresser.
我在摆弄她梳妆台上的东西。

417
00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:42.910
So I'm not really paying attention.
所以我其实没怎么注意。

418
00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:45.190
Her voice went from muffled, muffled, muffled back to clear.
她的声音从闷声闷气、闷声闷气、闷声闷气又变回了清晰。

419
00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:46.870
And so I look up.
于是我抬起头。

420
00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:53.550
Except she had changed the routine and had come out of the closet not completely dressed.
结果她改变了惯例，从衣帽间出来时并没有完全穿好衣服。

421
00:23:54.650 --> 00:23:57.490
In her sweatshirt, sweatpants, and bra.
穿着运动衫、运动裤和胸罩。

422
00:23:57.930 --> 00:24:02.270
And she was very easy on the eyes.
而且她长得非常养眼。

423
00:24:04.150 --> 00:24:04.670
Okay?
对吧？

424
00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:12.790
So now in that moment, I'm saying to myself, don't stare.
所以现在那一刻，我在心里对自己说，别盯着看。

425
00:24:13.470 --> 00:24:14.470
You're staring.
你在盯着看呢。

426
00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:15.650
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

427
00:24:15.650 --> 00:24:16.590
Look at her eyes.
看看她的眼睛。

428
00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:17.430
They're higher.
它们往上看呢。

429
00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:22.290
And so I'm, you know, having a little bit of gay freak out.
所以你知道的，我有点同性恋式的惊慌失措。

430
00:24:22.790 --> 00:24:29.010
And so, but we regulated, went to dinner, and everything got normal once everybody had their clothes back on.
不过呢，我们调整好了情绪去吃了晚饭，等大家都重新穿好衣服后一切就都恢复正常了。

431
00:24:30.230 --> 00:24:31.890
So, you know, super cool.
所以呢，你知道的，超级酷。

432
00:24:31.890 --> 00:24:37.110
And I, she was just really a, just a great person.
而且我，她真的是一个，绝对是个很好的人。

433
00:24:37.570 --> 00:24:39.130
Our friendship was so enjoyable.
我们的友谊是那么令人愉快。

434
00:24:40.090 --> 00:24:44.270
And yet, that's the casualty of being a lesbian, right?
然而，这就是身为女同的代价，对吧？

435
00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:45.530
Is the chemistry.
也就是那种化学反应。

436
00:24:46.850 --> 00:24:49.210
Women are so cool and dope.
女同胞们太酷太棒了。

437
00:24:52.220 --> 00:24:54.620
It's really easy to fall for you guys.
要爱上你们简直太容易了。

438
00:24:54.820 --> 00:24:58.600
It's just, the hard part is finding out the appropriate person to fall in love with.
只是，难点在于找到合适的对象去坠入爱河。

439
00:24:58.600 --> 00:25:05.520
But, and I'm not going to lie, I slept with a few varying genders in college, meaning straight women.
但是，说实话，我在大学里和几种不同性别的人睡过，也就是指异性恋女性。

440
00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:08.020
But she was not one of them.
但她不是其中之一。

441
00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.920
And then, after college, we lost touch.
然后，大学毕业后，我们就失联了。

442
00:25:11.200 --> 00:25:14.100
And recently, she started following me on Instagram.
最近，她开始在Instagram上关注我。

443
00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:19.140
And then, more recently, DM'd me that she was coming into New York and wanted to meet up.
再后来，她发私信给我说她要来纽约，想见个面。

444
00:25:20.020 --> 00:25:28.040
And I went to the place at the appointed time, and I was super curious about how it would feel to see her again.
我在约定好的时间去了那个地方，我超级好奇再次见到她会是什么感觉。

445
00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:37.260
I knew that she meant so much to me, but I also understand that what means something to you doesn't mean the same to somebody else.
我知道她对我很重要，但我也明白，对你来说意义重大的东西对别人来说可能并非如此。

446
00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:48.900
And then, suddenly, she was in front of me, and then she was in my arms, and I was in hers, and it was a great hug, a long hug, a strong hug.
然后，突然之间，她就站在我面前，接着她进了我的怀抱，我也抱住了她，那是一个很棒的拥抱，一个长久的拥抱，一个用力的拥抱。

447
00:25:49.020 --> 00:25:53.740
One of those hugs where you just rock side to side.
就是那种让你忍不住左右摇晃的拥抱。

448
00:25:54.580 --> 00:26:03.360
And then, we stopped, and we sat down, and we caught up, and we cried, and we laughed, and we held hands when shit was super hard to say.
然后，我们停下来，坐下，叙旧，哭泣，欢笑，当有些话极其难以说出口时，我们便紧紧握住彼此的手。

449
00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:05.720
And it was really beautiful.
那感觉真的很美妙。

450
00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:17.480
I could recognize it for what it was, a blinding, furious, and beautiful love that it was absolutely okay to have, and that was not in any way base.
我能认清它的本质，那是一种耀眼、炽热而美丽的爱，去拥有它是完全可以的，而且绝不低俗。

451
00:26:18.720 --> 00:26:25.920
And we're sitting there, and I'm telling her how much her friendship has meant to me, and then she flipped it and told me how much my friendship had meant to her,
我们当时坐在那儿，我告诉她她的友谊对我的意义有多重大，接着她话锋一转，告诉我我的友谊对她有多重要，

452
00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:34.200
and that she's not nostalgic, and she doesn't even have any pictures from college, but she has two that she's printed out, and one of them is of me.
她说她从不缅怀过去，甚至连大学的照片一张都没有，但她打印了两张照片，其中一张就是我。

453
00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:37.160
Yeah, I know, right?
对，我懂，是吧？

454
00:26:37.360 --> 00:26:43.920
And so, it was just so affirming in that moment to know that she was mine, and I was hers.
所以那一刻真的太让人肯定了，知道她是我的，我是她的。

455
00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:51.220
And if anyone ever asks me about the great loves of my life, she will be one that I talk about.
如果以后有人问起我生命中的挚爱，她绝对会是我提及的一个。

456
00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:52.700
Thank you.
谢谢你。

457
00:27:02.740 --> 00:27:04.200
That was Valerie Walker.
刚才那是瓦莱丽·沃克。

458
00:27:04.500 --> 00:27:11.620
She is an activist, artist, and storyteller whose stories challenge perceptions and build community through shared feelings.
她是一位活动家、艺术家和故事讲述者，她的故事通过共同的情感来挑战传统观念并建立社群。

459
00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:17.080
Survival as triumph and vulnerability as strength are key themes in her work.
将生存视作凯旋，将脆弱化为力量，是她作品中的核心主题。

460
00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:23.280
Our final story is from Matthew Dix, who told this at one of our open mic story slams in Boston.
我们的最后一个故事来自马修·迪克斯，这是他在波士顿的一次公开麦故事 slam 活动上讲的。

461
00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:25.960
Here's Matthew, live at the Moth.
有请马修，现场亮相“ Moth”故事会。

462
00:27:30.260 --> 00:27:34.720
I'm sitting in the break room of a McDonald's restaurant in Milford, Massachusetts.
我正坐在马萨诸塞州米尔福德一家麦当劳餐厅的员工休息室里。

463
00:27:34.720 --> 00:27:37.080
I'm eating an Egg McMuffin, and I am not happy.
我在吃一个满福堡，而且我非常不开心。

464
00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:39.900
It is the spring of 1987.
那是1987年的春天。

465
00:27:40.060 --> 00:27:44.060
I'm 16 years old, and it's not the Egg McMuffin that's causing me to be unhappy,
我16岁，让我不开心的并不是这个满福堡，

466
00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:48.900
because an Egg McMuffin is the most guaranteed source of joy in my entire day.
因为满福堡是我整天里最能确定获得快乐的源泉。

467
00:27:49.180 --> 00:27:50.360
But not on this day.
但今天不一样。

468
00:27:50.960 --> 00:27:54.900
I'm upset because I'm about to meet my mortal enemy for the first time,
我很烦躁，因为我马上要第一次见到我的死对头了，

469
00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:56.200
and I know it's not going to go well.
而且我知道这绝对不会顺利。

470
00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:58.880
I've been working at this restaurant for two months now.
我在这家餐厅已经工作两个月了。

471
00:27:59.040 --> 00:28:02.700
I actually live three towns away in Blackstone, Massachusetts,
其实我住在三个镇之外的马萨诸塞州布莱克斯通，

472
00:28:02.700 --> 00:28:07.500
but I found out that this place pays $4.65 an hour,
但我发现这里每小时工资4.65美元，

473
00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:11.380
and that's 20 cents more than the White Hen Pantry five minutes from my house.
比我家门口步行五分钟的 White Hen 便利店高出20美分。

474
00:28:11.380 --> 00:28:13.800
And I figured, even though it's a 30-minute drive,
我想着，虽然要开车30分钟，

475
00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:17.840
the 20 cents will absolutely make up for the time and the gas, which it does not.
但这多出来的20美分绝对能补回时间和油钱，然而事实并非如此。

476
00:28:18.280 --> 00:28:21.740
But it changes my life in a really significant way,
但它以一种非常重大的方式改变了我的生活，

477
00:28:21.740 --> 00:28:26.220
because when I arrive here, I discover the joy of a clean slate.
因为当我来到这里时，我发现了全新开始的快乐。

478
00:28:26.580 --> 00:28:28.500
I'm growing up in a tiny town.
我在一个小得不行的镇上长大。

479
00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:32.140
82 kids are in my class, the same 82 kids I knew in kindergarten,
我的年级里有82个孩子，就是我从幼儿园就认识的那同82个孩子，

480
00:28:32.380 --> 00:28:34.060
and they remember everything.
他们记得所有的事情。

481
00:28:34.420 --> 00:28:36.940
And so when you want to be something different,
所以当你想要变得与众不同，

482
00:28:36.940 --> 00:28:38.940
or you decide you could be something better,
或者你决定自己可以变得更好时，

483
00:28:38.940 --> 00:28:42.280
no one lets you because they remember everything.
根本没人会放过你，因为他们什么都记得。

484
00:28:42.540 --> 00:28:47.180
They still talk about the time in sixth grade when I exposed myself to class
他们到现在还在谈论六年级时我在全班面前走光的那次经历，

485
00:28:47.180 --> 00:28:49.760
because my gym shorts were a little too short,
因为我的运动短裤有点太短了，

486
00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:51.720
and my underwear was a little too big,
我的内裤有点太大了，

487
00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:54.520
and it was a little too much manspreading.
而且当时我的坐姿实在有点太开腿了。

488
00:28:54.680 --> 00:28:56.820
They talk about it to this day.
他们直到今天还在谈论这事。

489
00:28:57.360 --> 00:28:59.780
And they remember the braces and the buck teeth
他们还记得我的牙套、暴牙、

490
00:28:59.780 --> 00:29:02.060
and the bad haircuts and the free and reduced lunches,
糟糕的发型以及免费或减价午餐，

491
00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:05.200
and all of that has prevented me from becoming something
所有这些都阻止了我去成为一个

492
00:29:05.200 --> 00:29:09.640
that I think I could be and being trapped in what they think I should be.
我觉得自己能成为的人，而是让我被禁锢在他们认为我应该成为的样子里。

493
00:29:09.840 --> 00:29:11.480
But I've arrived in this new town.
但我来到了这个新镇子。

494
00:29:11.620 --> 00:29:12.360
Nobody knows me.
没有人认识我。

495
00:29:12.440 --> 00:29:15.480
And on the first day of work, Erin Duran comes and asks me if I have a girlfriend
在上班的第一天，埃琳·杜兰走过来问我有没有女朋友，

496
00:29:15.480 --> 00:29:17.160
and the way she's hoping I say no.
她问的时候那眼神是多么希望我说没有啊。

497
00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:19.020
And that's never happened to me before.
这在我身上还从来没发生过。

498
00:29:19.040 --> 00:29:20.020
So this is something.
所以这可真是一件大事。

499
00:29:20.480 --> 00:29:23.000
And it turns out that because they don't know me,
结果证明，因为他们不认识我，

500
00:29:23.200 --> 00:29:25.100
I can be the thing I think I can be.
我可以成为那个我觉得自己能成为的人。

501
00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:28.000
And suddenly I have more friends than I've ever had in my life.
突然之间，我的朋友比我这辈子任何时候都要多。

502
00:29:28.480 --> 00:29:30.200
And I'm good at my job.
而且我工作干得很出色。

503
00:29:30.860 --> 00:29:31.600
Shockingly good.
好得惊人。

504
00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:35.920
In the 1980s, the job at the McDonald's that is the hardest is running the bin.
在20世纪80年代，麦当劳最难干的活就是负责备餐区。

505
00:29:36.100 --> 00:29:38.560
I have been a public school teacher for 24 years,
我当了24年的公立学校教师，

506
00:29:38.580 --> 00:29:42.000
and I can tell you that I have not had a day in my classroom
我可以告诉你，在我的教室里，没有哪一天

507
00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:47.220
as taxing as a day running the bin at McDonald's during rush hour in 1987.
会像1987年麦当劳的高峰期在备餐区忙碌一天那样累人。

508
00:29:47.860 --> 00:29:53.220
It is coordinating a kitchen full of 16-year-olds and 60-year-olds
这需要统筹一个既有16岁青少年又有60岁老人的厨房，

509
00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:56.120
and convincing them all to do work for you at the same time
说服他们所有人同时为你干活，

510
00:29:56.120 --> 00:29:59.900
and watching a drive-through screen and listening to cash registers
还要盯着得来速屏幕，听着收银机的声音，

511
00:29:59.900 --> 00:30:02.840
and figuring out how much food needs to be here at any moment
计算在任何时候这里需要多少食物，

512
00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:05.180
without causing waste and making sure a profit.
既不造成浪费，又能确保盈利。

513
00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:06.280
It's really hard.
这真的很难。

514
00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:08.900
And for some reason, I can hold all this information right here
不知为什么，我能把所有这些信息全都装在脑子里，

515
00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:11.640
and I'm good at it and people respect me for it.
而且我干得很出色，大家都很尊敬我。

516
00:30:11.720 --> 00:30:15.300
But as soon as I got good at it, all I heard was one word, Benji.
但就在我刚做好的时候，我听到的只有一个名字：本吉。

517
00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:17.900
You're great, but Benji's better.
你很棒，但本吉更棒。

518
00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:20.300
Benji's the best bin person in this restaurant.
本吉是这家餐厅里最会负责备餐区的人。

519
00:30:20.460 --> 00:30:22.200
Actually, he's the best person in this restaurant.
事实上，他是这家餐厅里最棒的人。

520
00:30:22.460 --> 00:30:26.460
He is fantastic and everyone loves him and everyone respects him.
他太棒了，所有人都喜欢他，所有人都尊敬他。

521
00:30:26.460 --> 00:30:27.800
And I hate Benji.
而我讨厌本吉。

522
00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:30.820
All they do is tell me how great he is
他们一直在跟我说他有多优秀，

523
00:30:30.820 --> 00:30:33.280
and with every single word they say, I hate him more.
他们每多说一个字，我就更恨他一分。

524
00:30:33.380 --> 00:30:35.640
And then I discover they're telling him about me
然后我发现他们也在跟他提起我，

525
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:38.240
and they're saying how this guy came in
他们说这家伙来了，

526
00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:39.620
and he might be better than you.
而且他可能比你还厉害。

527
00:30:39.740 --> 00:30:42.120
They're spreading gossip about me to him
他们把关于我的八卦传给他听，

528
00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:45.000
and so we have never met each other, but we hate each other.
所以我们虽然从未谋面，但我们恨透了对方。

529
00:30:45.640 --> 00:30:48.160
And so this day, we're coming together for the first time.
于是今天，我们要第一次碰面了。

530
00:30:48.280 --> 00:30:50.180
Our shifts are crossing and I'm going to meet him.
我们的班次重合了，我要去见他。

531
00:30:50.520 --> 00:30:53.180
And so I go out into the dining room at the end of my break
所以我在休息结束时走到餐厅大堂，

532
00:30:53.180 --> 00:30:55.480
just to see him because he's already working and I see him.
就为了去看看他，因为他已经在工作了，我看到了他。

533
00:30:55.680 --> 00:30:57.080
There's nothing to this guy.
这家伙平平无奇。

534
00:30:57.240 --> 00:30:58.860
Like he's not that good looking.
长相也没那么出众。

535
00:30:58.860 --> 00:30:59.720
He's not an athlete.
也不是什么运动员。

536
00:30:59.900 --> 00:31:02.380
He's got the body of a bass player
他有着那种贝斯手的身材，

537
00:31:02.380 --> 00:31:04.520
and a failing high school rock band.
来自一支快要解散的高中摇滚乐队。

538
00:31:04.660 --> 00:31:05.380
He has nothing.
他什么也没有。

539
00:31:06.760 --> 00:31:09.220
But I watch and a couple minutes later,
但看着看着，几分钟后，

540
00:31:09.220 --> 00:31:13.580
I realize I'm wrong because he's funny, effortlessly funny.
我意识到自己想错了，因为他很有趣，那种不费吹灰之力的幽默。

541
00:31:13.900 --> 00:31:15.920
And he's endearing to everyone.
而且他极具亲和力，对每个人都很好。

542
00:31:16.080 --> 00:31:18.600
He makes the older customers who are waiting for Big Macs
他让那些在等巨无霸的老年顾客

543
00:31:18.600 --> 00:31:20.780
actually happy to be waiting for their Big Mac.
居然觉得等巨无霸也是一件开心的事。

544
00:31:20.780 --> 00:31:24.260
And the managers love him and he's good at the bin.
经理们也喜欢他，而且他备餐区的活干得极好。

545
00:31:24.520 --> 00:31:26.960
Like he is really good at calling bin.
他是真的非常擅长负责备餐区。

546
00:31:27.720 --> 00:31:29.540
I hate him so much.
我太恨他了。

547
00:31:30.260 --> 00:31:32.020
And because he's doing my job,
而且因为他在干我的活，

548
00:31:32.040 --> 00:31:33.520
I have to run for drive-thru today,
我今天得去负责得来速车道，

549
00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:35.240
which is the second hardest job in the restaurant.
这是餐厅里第二难的工作。

550
00:31:35.400 --> 00:31:37.060
80% of the orders go through the window.
80%的订单都是通过那个窗口完成的。

551
00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:39.700
So 80% of the food will pass through my hands.
所以百分之八十的食物都要经我的手。

552
00:31:39.820 --> 00:31:42.540
But that means I need to work with the bin guy the whole time
但这就意味着我得全程跟负责垃圾箱的家伙合作，

553
00:31:42.540 --> 00:31:45.340
to coordinate and negotiate and make sure everything runs,
去协调、交涉并确保一切运转顺畅，

554
00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:47.200
which means I have to work with Benji.
也就是说，我得和本吉合作。

555
00:31:47.660 --> 00:31:51.340
And so for the first hour, we don't talk to each other unless it's about work.
所以在第一个小时里，除了工作上的事，我们一句话也不说。

556
00:31:51.460 --> 00:31:53.000
And we clearly hate each other.
而且我们显然都讨厌对方。

557
00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:55.000
We're not hiding it in any way whatsoever.
我们根本没有做任何掩饰。

558
00:31:55.320 --> 00:31:57.700
But unless it has to do with work, I don't say a word.
但只要不是工作相关的事，我一个字都不会说。

559
00:31:58.140 --> 00:32:00.100
And then after an hour, it gets like awkward.
一个小时过去后，气氛就变得有些尴尬了。

560
00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:03.920
And I start to think maybe he thinks I'm afraid to say something to him.
我开始琢磨，也许他觉得我是不敢跟他说什么。

561
00:32:04.020 --> 00:32:05.640
So I'm like, no, I'm going to do something here.
于是我想，不行，我得在这儿做点什么。

562
00:32:05.880 --> 00:32:07.420
And so I go up to him and I say,
然后我走到他跟前说：

563
00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:10.120
why are you coming in at 10.30 on a Saturday?
你周六为什么十点半才来？

564
00:32:10.240 --> 00:32:10.960
What's 10.30?
十点半怎么了？

565
00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:13.840
And he says, I watch Saturday morning cartoons,
他说，我要看周六早上的动画片，

566
00:32:14.320 --> 00:32:15.980
which in 1986 is a thing.
这在1986年可是件大事。

567
00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:18.600
All the new cartoons, the Smurfs and the Snorks and Super Friends,
所有的新动画片，比如《蓝精灵》、《海底小精灵》和《超级朋友》，

568
00:32:18.760 --> 00:32:19.880
they're all out in the morning.
它们全都是在早上播出的。

569
00:32:20.200 --> 00:32:23.920
And we eat sugar disguised as cereal and we watch these things.
我们吃着伪装成麦片的糖，然后看着这些节目。

570
00:32:24.620 --> 00:32:28.740
And he says, the gummy bears start at 9.30 and they end at 10.
他说，《小熊维尼》（注：此处实际指Gummy Bears/弹跳小熊软糖历险记）九点半开始，十点结束。

571
00:32:28.740 --> 00:32:29.820
And then I come to work.
然后我就来上班了。

572
00:32:30.120 --> 00:32:32.760
And he says it without irony or embarrassment.
而且他说这话时既没有反讽，也没有不好意思。

573
00:32:32.760 --> 00:32:33.920
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

574
00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:37.460
And so I walk over to the drive-thru.
于是我走向得来速窗口。

575
00:32:37.580 --> 00:32:38.280
I drop a bag off.
放下了一袋东西。

576
00:32:38.360 --> 00:32:40.360
And when I come back to the bin, I say, listen to me.
当我回到垃圾箱旁时，我对他说：听着。

577
00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:44.760
Dashing and daring, courageous and caring,
勇猛顽强、勇敢热忱，忠诚友善、妙趣横生，

578
00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:47.980
faithful and friendly with stories to share.
（歌词：有故事要与大家分享。）

579
00:32:48.140 --> 00:32:50.600
And I take some food and I walk back to the drive-thru.
接着我拿了些食物，又走回得来速窗口。

580
00:32:51.020 --> 00:32:54.320
And as I come back over, he is singing before I get to the bin.
当我再次走回来时，我还没到垃圾箱旁他就唱了起来。

581
00:32:54.480 --> 00:32:57.980
He says, all through the forest, they sing out in chorus,
他说：穿过整片森林，它们齐声合唱，

582
00:32:58.300 --> 00:33:00.960
marching along as their songs fill the air.
迈着整齐的步伐，歌声响彻云霄。

583
00:33:01.740 --> 00:33:04.100
And standing next to the bin with Benji,
然后我和本吉一起站在垃圾箱旁，

584
00:33:04.360 --> 00:33:07.480
we sing together, gummy bears,
我们一起唱着， gummy bears（小熊软糖），

585
00:33:08.200 --> 00:33:10.500
bouncing here and there and everywhere.
这里蹦蹦，那里跳跳，到处都是。

586
00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:13.640
High adventure that's beyond compare.
无与伦比的惊险冒险。

587
00:33:14.080 --> 00:33:15.940
They are the gummy bears.
它们就是小熊软糖。

588
00:33:17.240 --> 00:33:20.080
There's a second verse, a bridge, and another chorus.
还有第二段歌词、过渡段和另一个副歌。

589
00:33:20.100 --> 00:33:23.320
I will not share them with you, but we sing them that day.
我不会唱给你们听，但我们那天确实唱了。

590
00:33:24.060 --> 00:33:26.240
Because I watch the gummy bears too.
因为我也看小熊软糖。

591
00:33:26.440 --> 00:33:28.560
And to this day, I can sing that song.
直到今天，我依然能唱出那首歌。

592
00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:30.440
And that's it.
就这样。

593
00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:36.340
A single theme song to a cartoon melts all the ice between us.
一部动画片的主题曲瞬间融化了我们之间的坚冰。

594
00:33:37.000 --> 00:33:41.460
And 37 years later, he is still my best friend.
37年后的今天，他依然是我最好的朋友。

595
00:33:43.040 --> 00:33:46.600
It is the most significant relationship in my life,
这是我生命中最重大的关系，

596
00:33:46.620 --> 00:33:48.320
with the exception of my marriage.
除了我的婚姻之外。

597
00:33:48.880 --> 00:33:51.260
When I get thrown out of my house when I'm 17,
在我17岁被赶出家门时，

598
00:33:52.040 --> 00:33:54.680
Benji takes me in and lets me live in his college apartment.
本吉收留了我，让我在他的大学公寓里住。

599
00:33:55.040 --> 00:33:58.260
And when I'm 21 and I need a credit card and can't get one,
而在我21岁需要一张信用卡却申请不到时，

600
00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:00.620
he gives me his extra card and says,
他把自己的副卡给了我，并说：

601
00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:02.600
just use it and pay me when you can.
尽管用吧，等你有钱了再付我钱。

602
00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:06.380
He saves my life again and again and again.
他一次又一次地救了我的命。

603
00:34:06.740 --> 00:34:08.760
And this day, we live in Connecticut,
而今天，我们住在康涅狄格州，

604
00:34:08.760 --> 00:34:10.440
two miles from each other.
相距仅两英里。

605
00:34:11.580 --> 00:34:14.760
And when I think back on that day that I stood at that bin
每当我回想起那天我站在那个垃圾桶旁，

606
00:34:14.760 --> 00:34:17.500
and sang a cartoon song to him,
对他唱着动画片歌曲的情景，

607
00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:22.300
I'm reminded how little it takes
我就会想起向某人伸出援手，

608
00:34:22.300 --> 00:34:25.760
to sort of reach out to someone
哪怕只是微微推开一扇窗户的缝隙，

609
00:34:25.760 --> 00:34:29.380
and just open the crack of a window.
其实是多么容易的一件事。

610
00:34:29.800 --> 00:34:32.640
And you just get the window open
只要你能把窗户推开一条缝，

611
00:34:32.640 --> 00:34:34.600
and then it becomes a door
它就会变成一扇门，

612
00:34:34.600 --> 00:34:36.460
and it becomes a lifetime.
进而成就一生的情谊。

613
00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:37.780
Thank you.
谢谢大家。

614
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:47.080
That was Matthew Dix.
刚才那是马修·迪克斯。

615
00:34:47.080 --> 00:34:49.760
He's an elementary school teacher and novelist
他是一名小学教师兼小说家，

616
00:34:49.760 --> 00:34:52.500
whose books include Memoirs of an Imaginary Friend,
他的作品包括《我的虚构朋友回忆录》、

617
00:34:52.860 --> 00:34:53.740
Something Missing,
《丢失的东西》

618
00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.540
and Unexpectedly Milo.
以及《意料之外的米洛》。

619
00:34:55.700 --> 00:34:58.460
He's the founder and creative director of Speak Up,
他是“大声说出来”（Speak Up）的创始人兼创意总监，

620
00:34:58.700 --> 00:35:00.820
a Hartford-based storytelling organization.
这是一个总部位于哈特福德的故事讲述组织。

621
00:35:01.320 --> 00:35:02.820
Matt loves ice cream cake,
马特喜欢冰淇淋蛋糕、

622
00:35:03.020 --> 00:35:03.860
tickling his children,
逗他的孩子们笑、

623
00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:05.160
staring at his wife,
凝视他的妻子，

624
00:35:05.360 --> 00:35:06.520
and not sleeping.
以及不睡觉。

625
00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:09.400
That brings us to the end of our episode.
我们的节目到这里就接近尾声了。

626
00:35:09.780 --> 00:35:12.640
Thank you to our storytellers for sharing with us
感谢我们的讲述者与我们分享故事，

627
00:35:12.640 --> 00:35:14.160
and to you for listening.
也感谢收听节目的你们。

628
00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:16.920
We hope that this week and every week,
我们希望在本周以及未来的每一个星期里，

629
00:35:17.060 --> 00:35:18.400
your friends are there for you.
你们的朋友都能陪伴在你们身边。

630
00:35:20.800 --> 00:35:23.040
Chloe Salmon is a director at The Moth.
克洛伊·萨尔蒙是“飞蛾”故事会（The Moth）的一名总监。

631
00:35:23.220 --> 00:35:25.280
Her favorite moth moments come on show days
她最喜欢的飞蛾时刻发生在演出当天，

632
00:35:25.280 --> 00:35:26.400
when the cardio is done,
当时彩排已经结束，

633
00:35:26.660 --> 00:35:27.800
the house lights go down,
剧场灯光暗下，

634
00:35:28.020 --> 00:35:29.380
and the magic settles in.
魔幻的时刻悄然降临。

635
